<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mehmed Pasha Bushati</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1775</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mehmed Pasha Bushati was an Ottoman Albanian governor, from a powerful family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Shkodër</a>, who was appointed governor of the sanjak of Scutari in 1757. He made the post hereditary in practice and founded the semi-independent Pashalik of Scutari, which his son Kara Mahmud Pasha expanded into the strongest power in northern Albania.</p></div>
